11. Many functions in the C++ standard library operate with iterators. An iterator is a variable
    that points to an element in a data structure.The often used iterators begin and end define
    a range that contains all elements in a data structure. The iterator begin points to the first 
    element in the data structure, and the iterator end points to the position after the last element.
    
    
12. `Sorting and reversing normal array ` : Ex: int a[n];
	1. `sort(a, a+n); ` : first parameter is the name of the array and second parameter is name 
	of a + n(number of elements of array a you wanted to operate on).
	2. `reverse(a, a+n);` : first parameter is the name of the array and second parameter is name of 
	a + n(number of elements of array a you wanted to operate on).
	
	
